// Fonts for the characters our own fonts don't draw, Japanese above all, tried in order.
// Each is a TrueType or OpenType file shipped unmodified with its licence beside it.
//
// A smooth font (just a `file`) is what text falls back to for the CJK scripts, drawn as it
// is at the text's size and smoothed; text with none of those characters stays crisp.
// A pixel-outline font (with `pixels_per_em`, the pixel grid it is drawn on) is instead read
// once at startup and merged under the chosen font on the same baseline (see
// `voxmar_texgen::font::import`), so only what that font lacks comes from it.
// `scale` (1 unless given) is how big a pixel font's pixels are drawn, in ours.
[
    // Kana and kanji in Fusion Pixel 12px, its pixels drawn three quarters the size of
    // ours: kanji about as tall as a 9-pixel font's, with all of their 12 pixels' detail.
    (file: "japanese/fusion-pixel-12px-monospaced-ja.ttf", pixels_per_em: 12, scale: 0.75),
    // Smooth, for any Japanese character it lacks.
    (file: "japanese/BIZUDGothic-Regular.ttf"),
]
